From d2fdacd98aec6deeda34a462988275bd2cea4570 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 16:58:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Skip unchanged sync-loop chat-link passes and pin
 placement config per round

reconcile_links ran every 60 s unconditionally: each pass re-ran
kanban_chat_links.reconcile and its creator-chats backfill over every task,
subscription, ledger row and replica link, and every placeholder check
reloaded the placement config (5051 loads per pass on a 600-card probe board).

- reconcile_links(skip_unchanged=True), used by run_forever, skips a board
  whose inputs equal its last completed pass: live file identity +
  kanban_activity_revision (transactional, covers tasks/events/subs/links,
  ignores bookkeeping columns), replica identity + feed cursor (read through
  the loop's pooled, generation-recovered handle), this gateway's ledger rows
  for the board (by value), mode, gateway/profile/home and placement config.
  Inputs are read before the pass, so a commit during it (including the
  pass's own writes) re-arms the next pass; a failed pass records nothing.
  LINKS_MAX_AGE_S (300 s) bounds the unkeyed state.db machine-session input.
  Explicit callers (hermes kanban sync links) still always reconcile.
- Boards are borrowed through the existing connection_scope pool.
- kanban_placement.config_snapshot pins one placement load per sync round
  and links pass (thread-local, nested-safe); config() honours it.

Probe (thread CPU, unchanged rounds, 600 / 1500 cards): links pass
303 -> 15 ms / 822 -> 47 ms; sync_board + links 310 -> 22 ms / 845 -> 66 ms;
links rows identical before/after.
